BT 1 0 0 1 0 43 Tm 13 TL /F2 9 Tf .117647 .160784 .231373 rg (1.1 What is COSMOSCOPE?) Tj /F1 9 Tf  T* (COSMOSCOPE is an open-science astronomical exploration and scientific analysis platform built for the NASA Space Apps) Tj T* (Challenge. It provides intuitive, browser-based tools that unlock genuine multi-epoch infrared observations captured by NASA's) Tj T* (revolutionary SPHEREx space telescope.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 621.8898 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 69 Tm 13 TL /F2 9 Tf .117647 .160784 .231373 rg (1.2 What Scientific Problem Does It Address?) Tj /F1 9 Tf  T* (Modern all-sky space telescopes generate petabytes of complex, multi-extension FITS data containing hundreds of spectral) Tj T* (channels and multiple observation dates. Historically, analyzing these multi-dimensional surveys required specialized) Tj T* (astrophysics software, command-line scripts, and large local compute clusters. COSMOSCOPE removes these technical) Tj T* (barriers by providing a responsive, zero-install research workbench where users can explore the dynamic infrared universe in) Tj T* (real time.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 551.8898 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 56 Tm 13 TL /F2 9 Tf .117647 .160784 .231373 rg (1.3 What is the SPHEREx Mission?) Tj /F1 9 Tf  T* (SPHEREx \() Tj /F3 9 Tf (Spectro-Photometer for the History of the Universe, Epoch of Reionization and Ices Explorer) Tj /F1 9 Tf (\) is a NASA) Tj T* (Medium-Class Explorer \(MIDEX\) mission designed to conduct the first-ever all-sky near-infrared spectrophotometric survey.) Tj T* -0.106801 Tw (Operating in a 650 km Sun-synchronous low-Earth polar orbit, SPHEREx maps the entire celestial sphere every 6 months across) Tj T* 0 Tw /F2 9 Tf (102 narrow spectral bands) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( from ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (0.75 \265m to 5.0 \265m) Tj /F1 9 Tf (.) Tj T* ET
