BT 1 0 0 1 0 108 Tm 13 TL /F2 9 Tf .117647 .160784 .231373 rg (7.1 FITS Processing & Astronomical Stretches:) Tj /F1 9 Tf  T* (Astronomical images have immense dynamic range\227a bright star can be 100,000 times brighter than the background. To reveal) Tj T* (faint details without saturating bright pixels, the Image Analysis Lab supports five stretches:) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Linear:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( Direct scaling, best for uniform bright fields.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Logarithmic:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( Compresses high-flux cores to reveal faint outer nebular structures.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Asinh \(Inverse Hyperbolic Sine\):) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( Smoothly transitions from linear at the noise floor to logarithmic at high intensities,) Tj T* (preserving stellar profiles without blowing out cores.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Square Root:) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( Balanced compression commonly used in optical astronomy.) Tj  T* (\177 ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (ZScale \(IRAF Standard\):) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( Automatically samples pixel variance to optimize contrast around the sky noise floor.) Tj T* ET
